  "_about": "the house cat SCULPTED on the big-cat frame at s = .22 (2026-11-05, gen: scratchpad sc/carn/gen/cat.py from the tiger's body): 25 cm at the shoulder, 47 cm head-body, slim and a little longer in the leg than a tiger, the tail carried up; a round short-faced head with big forward eyes and big upright ears. Its colours are the coat's keys (its `coats`: species.js makeCat builds each from this file) (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): one cupped sheet each (sharp.js `fin`), an upright triangle with full sides and a round tip, the hollow pink inside a band of fur, the root faired into the head. (2026-11-08) The CHEEK's tabby lines back from the eye (its own frame, sc/carn/gen/cat.py): below the ear that frame meets the skull's and the neck's, three at once, which bodymesh.js now paints in three slots per vertex (patternsMesh) -- the lines run on clean there, no stair-stepped terraces. WHISKERS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sharp/whiskers.py): 12 white whiskers a side, 4 rows on the whisker pad (40-60 mm); 3 white whiskers a side, a brow tuft (19-26 mm) -- `whiskers` shapes (bodyspec.js whiskerStrands: thin pointed strands, mirrored, on the head, near mesh only; details, so every coat and variant still shares one mesh). (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/tails.py) The TAIL is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along its bones, not a chain of cones blended one into the next: no beads, its thin end exact rings. (`thin` 3.2 set by hand: under 3.2 cells across it is drawn as rings, the tip rounded.)",
